  "notes": "Fully self-produced EDM/electroclash-rage — four-on-the-floor and electro kick sections alternating with trap grids, aggressive sidechain pump, crisp EDM claps against trap snares. ⛔ **The research says the low end is a reese/FM growl rather than an 808, and `reese_sustain` is exactly the rhythm this engine cannot use**: `bass.rs` emits one note per chord on it (TASK-162), so a growl authored that way is one held note for the whole clip. It is written as `independent_riff` over a fast arpeggiated register instead, which is what the growl actually plays; the timbre is the sound designer's half, not the generator's. ⚠ The 808 is kept sparse rather than absent — the model still has to write a low part. ⚠ The countermelody is deliberately sparse and NOT `fillGapsOnly`: a 16th-note arp melody leaves no gaps, so a gap-filling counter wrote nothing at all and `coverage.rs` caught the model promising a part it does not write.",
